From 66414241114fa34fce27c195c2fb2d2743e41f8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keptn42 <keptn42@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:43:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] draft: an adaptive draft window per sequence
 (RADIANCE_DRAFT_ADAPT)

One depth for every request is too shallow for code and JSON and too deep
for prose. With RADIANCE_DRAFT_ADAPT=1, --num-speculative-tokens becomes
the ceiling and each sequence drafts into the window d that maximises
E(d)/T(d): the tokens a step is expected to emit from the sequence's own
smoothed acceptance at each position, over the step's cost
(RADIANCE_DRAFT_COST, depth:ms pairs). The serial head runs as many rounds
as the deepest window in the step. A window moves only past a hysteresis
and a hold, since a new window is a new pass shape. Acceptance is
unchanged. /metrics gains radiance:draft_depth_adaptive and
radiance:draft_verify_depth_total{depth} while it is on. Unset, nothing
changes. Greedy at up to 6 against fixed 3: code +7.7 %, JSON +16.3 %.
---
