From d229d24f97b2e5078239a0a000a3b92e1183a638 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keptn42 <keptn42@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:40:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] draft: cap every adaptive window under load
 (RADIANCE_DRAFT_ADAPT_BUSY)

The cost table prices a step at one sequence. Under load every row a step
adds is expert bandwidth its neighbours wait on, and the adaptive window
lost 4 % at 8 concurrent requests. With RADIANCE_DRAFT_ADAPT_BUSY=N and
more than N sequences running, every window is capped at
RADIANCE_DRAFT_ADAPT_BUSY_DEPTH (default 3); the estimates keep learning.
The count is taken once a cycle and held to its end, so the plan, the
rounds, expect_draft and set_draft see one cap. Unset, nothing changes.
